<!-- TPO MAINTENANCE & COMMON MISTAKES -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#F7F7F7;border-top:1px solid #E0E0E0">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <p class="sl gp mb-3">TPO Care Guide</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1rem">TPO ROOF MAINTENANCE &amp; COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID</h2>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto">A properly maintained TPO roof lasts 20-30 years in Florida. Skip maintenance and the same roof fails in year 10-12. Here's the practical schedule and the mistakes we see cost Tampa Bay building owners the most.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
      <!-- MAINTENANCE SCHEDULE -->
      <div style="background:#F7F7F7;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:14px;padding:1.75rem 1.75rem 1.5rem">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.65rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(230,168,23,.12);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"/></svg></div>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.15rem;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:.02em;margin:0">MAINTENANCE SCHEDULE</h3>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.85rem">
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#E6A817;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .2rem">Quarterly</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Ground-level visual for punctures, blisters, seam separation, and standing water. Clear all drains, scuppers, and downspouts. Blocked drainage is the #1 cause of premature TPO failure in Florida.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#E6A817;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .2rem">Semi-Annual</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Check flashings and sealants around HVAC units, vents, skylights, and any roof penetrations for cracks or lifting.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#E6A817;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .2rem">Annual (Pre-Hurricane, May)</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Professional inspection of every heat-welded seam for creep or opening. Required to protect most material warranties.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#E6A817;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .2rem">Annual (Post-Hurricane, Nov/Dec)</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Full assessment of any wind damage, uplift, or debris impact.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#E6A817;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 .2rem">Every 3-5 Years</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Consider a manufacturer-approved TPO coating or restoration. Can add 8 to 10 years to membrane life if applied before failure.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- COMMON MISTAKES -->
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid rgba(232,65,90,.25);border-radius:14px;padding:1.75rem 1.75rem 1.5rem">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.65rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(232,65,90,.1);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E8415A" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg></div>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.15rem;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:.02em;margin:0">COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID</h3>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.85rem">
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin:0 0 .2rem">1. Walking on TPO in high heat</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Surface temperatures exceed 150&deg;F on summer afternoons; foot traffic causes permanent indentations that become future leak paths. Schedule rooftop work for early morning.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin:0 0 .2rem">2. Ignoring ponding water past 48 hours</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">TPO under standing water deteriorates 3&times; faster than on properly drained slopes. Ponding = same-week drain check.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin:0 0 .2rem">3. Using solvent-based cleaners</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Degreasers, gasoline, and many industrial cleaners cause TPO to swell and lift. Use manufacturer-approved cleaners only (water + mild detergent).</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin:0 0 .2rem">4. Skipping annual professional inspection</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Small seam separations are the leading TPO failure mode and only visible up close. A DIY ground-level look misses them until year 5, when they're full leaks.</p></div>
          <div><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin:0 0 .2rem">5. DIY silicone caulk patches</p><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Silicone won't bond permanently to TPO. Patches require the correct primer + heat-welded TPO-compatible cover strips. DIY caulk fails within 6-12 months and often voids the manufacturer warranty.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:center;background:#F7F7F7;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem 2rem">
      <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0 0 .5rem"><strong>Happy Roof offers commercial TPO maintenance programs</strong> that cover the full schedule above on a documented cadence, typically more cost-effective than paying per visit, and required by most manufacturer material warranties.</p>
      <p style="color:#555;font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> for a maintenance proposal on your building.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

