<section class="py-20" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <p class="sl gt mb-3">Common Questions</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em">COMMERCIAL ROOFING FAQS</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        What Types of Commercial Roofing Does Happy Roof Install?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Happy Roof installs TPO (thermoplastic polyolefin), EPDM (ethylene propylene diene monomer), modified bitumen, built-up roofing (BUR), and standing seam metal roofing for commercial properties in Tampa Bay. We work with warehouses, retail centers, offices, multi-family buildings, HOA properties, and industrial facilities. Call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#5AAFE0;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> to discuss your project.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        How Long Does a Commercial Roof Replacement Take?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Generally speaking, it depends on the building's size and the system being installed. That said, a typical 10,000 square foot TPO or EPDM installation will usually take five to ten business days. We may recommend phasing larger or more complex projects to reduce any disruption.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        Do You Offer Warranties on Commercial Roofing?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Every flat roof installation, including TPO, EPDM, and modified bitumen, comes with our 10-year workmanship warranty in writing. Commercial metal roofing comes with up to a 15-year workmanship warranty. Both are backed by manufacturer material warranties of 20 to 30 years, depending on the system. Rest assured, you'll receive all of this in writing before we close out the job.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        Can You Work Around Our Business Hours to Minimize Disruption?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Definitely. We understand that operations don't stop for a roof, so we offer phased scheduling and early morning or weekend work windows for occupied buildings. We'll also always make sure to coordinate with you and any project managers or tenants before and during the project, so there are no surprises.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        Do You Handle Commercial Roof Maintenance and Inspections?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">We do. Happy Roof offers commercial inspection and preventative maintenance programs. We typically recommend scheduling inspections at least twice a year to catch things like membrane tears, ponding water, and flashing separation, among other things, before they end up turning into expensive repairs. It's also worth noting that most manufacturer warranties require documented maintenance to stay valid.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        What TPO Roof Maintenance Should Florida Commercial Building Owners Do?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">A Florida TPO roof needs a layered maintenance schedule to hit its 20-30 year lifespan. <strong>Quarterly:</strong> ground-level visual for punctures, blisters, seam separation, and standing water; clear all drains, scuppers, and downspouts (blocked drainage is the #1 cause of premature TPO failure in Florida). <strong>Semi-annual:</strong> check flashings and sealants around HVAC units, vents, skylights, and roof penetrations. <strong>Annual pre-hurricane (May):</strong> professional inspection of heat-welded seams for creep or opening. Required to protect most material warranties. <strong>Annual post-hurricane (Nov/Dec):</strong> full assessment of any wind damage. <strong>Every 3-5 years:</strong> consider a manufacturer-approved TPO coating or restoration. Can add 8 to 10 years to membrane life if applied before failure. Happy Roof's commercial maintenance program covers all of this on a documented schedule; call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#5AAFE0;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> for a proposal.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        What Are Some Common TPO Roof Maintenance Mistakes to Avoid?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">A few small mistakes actually account for the majority of premature TPO failures in Florida, including, but not limited to: <strong>Walking on TPO in high heat:</strong> surface temperatures can exceed 150 degrees on summer afternoons, and foot traffic causes permanent indentations that could become future leak points. <strong>Ignoring ponding water for more than 48 hours:</strong> standing water accelerates membrane deterioration by up to three times as quickly. <strong>Using solvent-based cleaners:</strong> degreasers, gasoline, and most industrial cleaners can cause TPO to swell and lift. We recommend using manufacturer-approved cleaners only, which typically consist of water and mild detergent. <strong>Skipping annual professional inspection:</strong> small seam separations are the most common TPO failure mode and can go undetected at ground level until they become full leaks. <strong>DIY silicone caulk patches:</strong> silicone doesn't permanently bond to TPO, and DIY caulk patches usually fail within 6-12 months; plus, they may void the manufacturer's warranty. TPO repairs generally require a specific primer and heat-welded, TPO-compatible cover strips.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
